# macOS-Specific Guidelines

## Permissions
- Request Screen Recording permission on first launch
- Request Accessibility permission if needed for hotkeys
- Provide clear instructions if permission denied
- Link to System Preferences when needed

## Menu Bar App Best Practices
- No dock icon (LSUIElement = true)
- Menu bar icon should be minimal and recognizable
- Respect macOS design guidelines
- Support dark mode

## Screen Capture
- Handle multiple displays correctly
- Support different color profiles
- Convert to sRGB for HEX representation
- Document color accuracy limitations

## Global Hotkeys
- Default: Cmd+Shift+C (non-conflicting)
- Allow customization
- Handle conflicts gracefully
- Provide alternative activation methods

## UI/UX Guidelines
- Minimal and clean design
- Fast and responsive
- Intuitive and discoverable
- Consistent with macOS design
- Support keyboard navigation
- Provide clear labels
- Support VoiceOver
- Follow macOS accessibility guidelines

## Critical Error Handling
- Screen capture failures: Check Screen Recording permission, verify display configuration
- Hotkey registration failures: Check permission status, verify registration, check for conflicts
- Permission denials: Provide clear user guidance and links to System Preferences
- Memory issues: Monitor memory usage, optimize caching strategies
